    },
    "body": "I think you need to update the underlying model, at https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#sandboxing . How this section of the spec works is that the keywords get parsed and mapped to a flag set, with some translation, in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#parse-a-sandboxing-directive:\r\n\r\n- Flags prevent things, whereas keywords allow things. So the flags get set, *unless* the keywords are present.\r\n\r\n- Some keywords are redundant or combine to create the underlying flags. E.g. both `allow-top-navigation` and `allow-top-navigation-by-user-activation` cause the [sandboxed top-level navigation with user activation browsing context flag](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#sandboxed-top-level-navigation-with-user-activation-browsing-context-flag) to be removed.\r\n\r\nSo I think you'll want some sort of \"sandboxed custom protocol handlers\" flag, which gets removed if any of `allow-top-navigation` or `allow-popups` or `allow-custom-protocols-navigation` are set.\r\n\r\nThe fact that \"hand-off to external software\" uses token keywords, instead of flag names, seems like a preexisting spec bug. The token keywords do not exist at this point, and are not the type of thing which a sandboxing flag set contains.\r\n\r\nI would offer to fix this so that you could build on a better foundation, but since you are going to change the logic here somewhat dramatically, I think it's best if you fix it as part of the same PR.",
    "state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED",
